seg-70343708da03 = From schema { "1.3" } inputs <c1/> also carries a <c2/> label (<c3/>, <c4/>, <c5/>) on each reason that came with one: the deduction's class at the latest epoch. The geometry series come after all the others and only once an input epoch carries <c6/> (live schema { "1.3" }, a result from engine { "0.36" } or later), so a { "0.35" } stream or result renders byte for byte as before. Label values are fixed sets (an unknown status reads <c7/>; an unknown class is dropped). Alert on <c8/> rather than on the band alone, so a poor sky does not page as an attack; a <c9/> class is a statement about the sky, not a finding that no attack occurred (see <c10/>).

